# {{DISPLAY_NAME}} clients for Crawlora

Official Crawlora client packages for the hosted {{DISPLAY_NAME}} API. These clients call Crawlora's hosted API; they do not scrape {{DISPLAY_NAME}} locally. Requests use your Crawlora account and `CRAWLORA_API_KEY`; service usage follows your account billing plan. Crawlora is independent from and not affiliated with or endorsed by {{DISPLAY_NAME}} or its owners.

- JavaScript / TypeScript: [`{{NPM_NAME}}`](javascript/README.md)
- Python: [`{{PYTHON_NAME}}`](python/README.md)
- Go: [`{{GO_MODULE}}`](go.mod)
- Ruby: [`{{GEM_NAME}}`](ruby/README.md)
- Java: [`{{MAVEN_COORDINATE}}`](java/README.md)
- PHP: [`{{COMPOSER_NAME}}`](php/README.md)
- [API endpoint and parameter reference](docs/usage.md)
- [Runnable examples](examples/)
- [Package repository]({{REPOSITORY}})

Create an account at [crawlora.net](https://crawlora.net/signup), open the [Crawlora console](https://crawlora.net/app) to get an API key, or read the [API documentation](https://crawlora.net/docs).

## Install

```sh
npm install {{NPM_NAME}}
python -m pip install {{PYTHON_NAME}}
go get {{GO_MODULE}}@latest
gem install {{GEM_NAME}}
composer require {{COMPOSER_NAME}}
```

For Java, add `{{MAVEN_COORDINATE}}` to your Maven dependencies; see [java/README.md](java/README.md).

Set your API key before running a client:

```sh
export CRAWLORA_API_KEY="your-crawlora-api-key"
```

Do not commit API keys. See each language README for runnable usage examples.

